{"id": "EUVD-2026-39283", "enisaUuid": "d8c80ffe-3bca-3e33-8ffa-c386f88a7810", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nALSA: timer: Fix UAF at snd_timer_user_params()\n\nAt releasing a timer object, e.g. when a userspace timer\n(CONFIG_SND_UTIMER) gets closed and snd_timer_free() is called, it\ntries to detach the timer instances and release the resources.\nHowever, it's still possible that other in-flight tasks are holding\nthe timer instance where the to-be-deleted timer object is associated,\nand this may lead to racy accesses.\n\nFortunately, most of ioctls dealing with the timer instance list\nalready have the protection with register_mutex, and this also avoids\nsuch races.  But, SNDRV_TIMER_IOCTL_PARAMS isn't protected, hence the\nconcurrent ioctl may lead to use-after-free.\n\nThis patch just adds the guard with register_mutex to protect\nsnd_timer_user_params() for covering the code path as a quick\nworkaround.  It's no hot-path but rather a rarely issued ioctl, so the\nperformance penalty doesn't matter.", "datePublished": "2026-06-25T08:39:03", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T19:57:27", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/38034d04d4a75bbca01df2b313ced0bcd0fa3242", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3d39da65b5c422c5e5afb7d5651b0698d060a827", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/306427adf9b97e29e5958cb9cf3096c6151fc9ff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/053a401b592be424fea9d57c789f66cd5d8cec11"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-53192", "GHSA-jmf6-3v74-7x28"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.1, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "1859537c-6d54-374d-b22f-f244b5666626", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "37745918e0e7575bc40f38da93a99b9fa6406224 <053a401b592be424fea9d57c789f66cd5d8cec11"}, {"id": "1d0e55c0-19bf-3fa3-836d-8c70310131b4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2183dd6c-a7a7-3c08-8083-15c434861506", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "37745918e0e7575bc40f38da93a99b9fa6406224 <306427adf9b97e29e5958cb9cf3096c6151fc9ff"}, {"id": "408f70b9-99f9-3197-9894-adbbf9828923", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "5a910585-5536-38b7-ba26-fac398bfae9b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.13"}, {"id": "77935644-aaa0-30f1-b1f8-52edd131b35d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.36"}, {"id": "9d84ced6-80c9-3c24-8ff8-f4412805110f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "37745918e0e7575bc40f38da93a99b9fa6406224 <38034d04d4a75bbca01df2b313ced0bcd0fa3242"}, {"id": "a0d3bef0-087e-3d86-88e4-ed44797d8832", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.94"}, {"id": "b9102ae3-4dee-3914-8af7-cf6562cf5a16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "37745918e0e7575bc40f38da93a99b9fa6406224 <3d39da65b5c422c5e5afb7d5651b0698d060a827"}, {"id": "de0423cd-511e-3c27-b746-c74f78551814", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "fcda5a59-766f-3cf5-a528-2fa39d367234", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}